Weave schema migrations
=======================

Alembic is the only supported schema creation and upgrade mechanism.
The API never calls SQLAlchemy metadata.create_all() and never stamps revisions.
The root revision 20260911_initial_schema is a frozen historical snapshot;
do not edit or regenerate it from application models. Use a new Alembic
revision for every subsequent schema change.

Railway deployment
------------------

For the Weave API service in EACH environment (staging and production), set
its Pre-Deploy Command to:

    python -m app.config.schema_migrations

The Railway root directory for these API services is /backend. The command
runs in the backend container and uses the environment's DATABASE_URL.
Normal API startup only verifies a complete, versioned schema at Alembic head.
Missing migrations block readiness instead of silently repairing or stamping.

The deployment entrypoint takes a PostgreSQL transaction-scoped advisory lock
shared with the startup schema gate. It rejects partial/unversioned schemas,
unknown Alembic revisions and missing frozen-baseline tables, runs 'upgrade
head' on the locked connection, and checks for model/schema drift before
committing. PostgreSQL DDL and revision updates remain in the same transaction.
If migration or drift validation fails, the transaction rolls back and Railway
must not start the new deployment. Existing API deployments can continue.

Existing databases
------------------

Do not use 'alembic stamp' to adopt an existing database automatically. Before
first activating the Railway command on a live environment, inspect its
alembic_version row, actual schema, backup/recovery status, and service target.
If it reports the historical root revision but has schema drift, stop and
reconcile explicitly; the revision number alone does not prove equivalence.

Run migrations in staging, verify health and CI, then promote the same
code to master/production separately. Expand-and-contract migrations are
required while previous and new API deployments may overlap.
